<%#
  The 401 body served to a speculative (prefetched) request for a /supervisor
  page. It exists because Turbo reuses a prefetched response for a click on the
  same link, so this is what would render if a link to the panel ever shipped
  without `data-turbo-prefetch="false"`.

  `data: { turbo: false }` on the link is what makes it useful: it forces a real
  browser navigation instead of a Turbo visit, and a real navigation gets the
  `WWW-Authenticate` challenge — which is the sign-in dialog, arriving because
  someone asked for it.

  Self-contained on purpose: rendered with `layout: false` from a before_action,
  with none of Administrate's view context set up.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <title>Sign in to Supervisor</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin:0;padding:1rem;box-sizing:border-box;font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;background:#f9fafb;color:#111827">
    <main style="max-width:32rem;margin:3rem auto;padding:1.5rem;box-sizing:border-box;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:0.5rem">
      <h1 style="margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:600">Sign in to Supervisor</h1>
      <p style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;color:#4b5563;line-height:1.5">
        The Supervisor panel is behind an HTTP Basic credential. Continue to be prompted for it.
      </p>
      <%= link_to "Continue to Supervisor",
            request.path,
            data: { turbo: false },
            style: "display:inline-block;padding:0.5rem 1rem;background:#4f46e5;color:#fff;border-radius:0.375rem;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:500" %>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
